----------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY & ACCEPTANCE
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Data sources (web → native, no HTTP in the view):
  • useTranslation → VersionSegmentStrings facade (P1/S10), NSLocalizedString table.
  • useChangelog   → VersionSegmentChangelogObserver (P1/S8): emits the unseen count (web
                     newEntries.length); NotificationChangelogObserver recomputes on the changelog-opened
                     broadcast (web useSyncExternalStore on storage events). openChangelogModal() →
                     NotificationCenter broadcast (web window.dispatchEvent CustomEvent).
  • useQuery('/system/version')      → VersionInfoProbe (P1/S8), polled at 60s (web refetchInterval).
  • useQuery('/system/update-check') → UpdateCheckProbe (P1/S8), polled at 1h (web refetchInterval).

States — every one renders (no hidden surface):
  loading (first version probe in flight, no version yet → skeleton pill) · empty (resolved, no version
  at all → friendly "Version unavailable" pill, never a blank box) · error (first probe failed with
  nothing cached → danger pill + retry) · ready (segment button + tooltip opening the modal) · stale +
  offline freshness chip in the modal (version-poll failure keeps cached value; one-shot auto-refresh on
  the stale transition). With a normal build (baked version or the `dev` worst-case) a version always
  resolves → `.ready`, byte-for-byte the web behaviour; the leaf states are reachable when the host bakes
  no build version, the same way NewVersionBanner (0129) surfaces the probe lifecycle the web folds away.

Web-source-specific branches reproduced exactly:
  • appVersion order: (server app_version && !== 'unknown') ? server : BUILD_VERSION || 'dev'.
  • sha = BUILD_SHA; `· {sha}` + Commit row shown only when sha !== 'dev'.
  • updateAvailable = !!updateCheck.update_available → amber dot + "newer release" banner (+ v{latest},
    + message).
  • hasUnseen (newEntries.length > 0) → cyan dot (only when no update) + tooltip "{count} new release(s)"
    + "What's new" unseen dot. Update dot wins over unseen (web order).
  • uptimeLabel(seconds): d/h/m flooring, nil for nil/non-finite/<=0 — byte-for-byte.
  • modal <dl>: App version + Commit always; Helm chart (chart_version && !== 'unknown'), Go runtime
    (go_version), Platform ([os,arch].filter(Boolean).join('/')), Server uptime — presence-guarded.
  • tooltip = "TeslaSync version · v{ver}[ · {sha}][ · up {uptime}][ · {count} new release(s)]".
  • aria-label = "TeslaSync version: v{ver}[ ({sha})][, unseen changelog]".
  • iconOnly prop honoured. Release notes → https://github.com/ev-dev-labs/teslasync/releases
    (host-opened via the onOpenReleaseNotes seam / NotificationCenter broadcast, web window.open).

i18n keys: 17 web keys present + resolved via the facade (no English literals in Swift):
  statusBar.version.{tooltip,aria,uptime,updateAvailable,modalTitle,appVersion,commit,chart,go,platform,
  uptimeLabel,updateBanner,changelog,close} + changelog.{unseenHint,unseenAria,openModal}.
  + 9 native P4-leaf/a11y keys (loadingA11y, unavailable, retryA11y, openHint, live, stale, offline,
  staleA11y, offlineA11y). Dead web keys: 0. Missing web keys: 0. (26/26 used == declared.)

Accessibility: the segment is one focusable button whose VoiceOver label is the web aria-label
(version + SHA + unseen) and whose value announces "Update available" (the web update-dot's own label);
the glyph + dots are decorative. The modal rows are combined elements; What's new / Release notes / Close
are individually-labelled TSButtons; the freshness chip is a labelled refresh button. Dynamic Type via
tokens; reduce-motion respected (no bespoke animation).

